## The third half of the `player` and `java-player` resources of pumpkin/src/plugin/loader/wasm/wasm_host/wit/v0_1/player.rs
## (pumpkin-wasm-host-v0_1/src/{player,inventory,advancement,status_effect}.rs of the newer tree for the methods the pinned
## host lacks): inventory, ender chest and hand items through `item-stack` handles, the `inventory` and `player-inventory`
## resources, `open-gui`, `open-book`, `set-display-name`, `delete-message-*`, status effects, advancements, ray tracing and
## projectiles, and the `java-player` methods that have a packet or a field behind them. `installPlayer3` is called by
## pluginhost.aowl after `installPlayer` (it needs the item-stack and gui state of the `WitExt`).
##
## An `item-stack` handle here owns a copy (`ItemStack` is a value in aowlmony; upstream's handle shares the `Arc` of the
## inventory slot): a plugin that changes a stack it got from `get-inventory-item` writes it back with
## `set-inventory-item`.
##
## A handle's rep: `player-inventory` is the player's entity id; `inventory` is `entityId * 4 + 1` for the main inventory
## (36 slots) and `+ 2` for the ender chest (27).
## PARTIAL: pumpkin/src/plugin/loader/wasm/wasm_host/wit/v0_1/player.rs - not done here: `java-player.send-packet` and
## `show-dialog` (the generated packet and dialog variants are not lowered; `clear-dialog` is), `get-scoreboard` answers the
## world's scoreboard handle, `launch-projectile` for arrow, splash-potion and trident answers none, the `bedrock-player` resource
## except `open-form`, `reset-scoreboard`, `get-ability`/`set-ability` (the shared `Abilities`) and the status flags (kept here per
## entity id: the `Entity` has no Bedrock flag words and nothing resends the metadata); `get-version`, `get-settings` and `send-packet`
## of `bedrock-player` are not done (the session's client data is not exposed to the plugin host). `get-world-players` is done.
## (`as-bedrock` answers none for a Java client).
